  "title": "Dancing Plague of 1518: Why Couldn't a Town Stop Dancing?",
  "description": "The dancing plague of 1518 began in Strasbourg when one woman stepped out and danced for days. Soon dozens joined her. Why couldn't they stop?\n\nIn July 1518, Frau Troffea started dancing in the street. Within weeks, dozens, maybe hundreds, of people in Strasbourg were dancing with her. Doctors blamed hot blood, and the city answered with more dancing: a stage was built and musicians were hired. It only got worse. Historian John Waller sees it as a mass psychogenic illness in a starving town that feared the curse of Saint Vitus.\n\nSubscribe to Stickstory for a strange true story every day. Would you have joined the dance or run away? Tell me in the comments!\n\n#shorts #dancingplague #history #stickstory",
